  "description": "Fix the project context, the vision and the roadmap (docs/phases.md steps 4 to 6). Every project context default (audience, source and target language, platform and operating systems, kind of thing, deployment and licence) is recorded as an assumption and checked; the context, the vision and the roadmap are each approved by a person. An approval is a record bound to the revision it decided, approved or rejected, produced only by an action that needs the authority owner.approve, once per revision; after a rejection the artifact's writer is admissible and its new revision is checked and approved again. A revised requirements list invalidates the context check; a revised vision invalidates the roadmap approval. The case ends passed once the roadmap is approved; nothing about epics or specifications happens before that. Late findings (docs/trial-2.md, \"The late-finding loop\"): the context check also runs the consistency rules of the context against the requirements list and reads the open findings, and is not valid while one is open; no vision or roadmap is written or approved then. amend.upstream resolves an open finding by amending the questions and the requirements list, which moves the requirements to a new revision, so the context check is observed again.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "description": "a person's decision on a context revision; its result is approved or rejected (the reasons of a rejection are the step's log, handed to the writer)",
      "name": "context_approval",
      "produced_by": [
        "context.approve"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "the context check: schema-valid, every field present and recorded as an assumption with its status, no consistency rule firing between the context and the requirements list, and no open finding; its result is valid, invalid or finding",
      "name": "context_defaults",
      "produced_by": [
        "context.check"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "a person's decision on a roadmap revision; its result is approved or rejected (the reasons of a rejection are the step's log, handed to the writer)",
      "name": "roadmap_approval",
      "produced_by": [
        "roadmap.approve"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "the result of `aep plan artifact validate` over the store holding the vision and the roadmap, valid or invalid",
      "name": "roadmap_validation",
      "produced_by": [
        "roadmap.validate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "a person's decision on a vision revision; its result is approved or rejected (the reasons of a rejection are the step's log, handed to the writer)",
      "name": "vision_approval",
      "produced_by": [
